//? Title: DeepLab atrous features and exact Potts refinement
//? Subtitle: Tensor computations, explicit checks and reproducible local figures
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Pixel labels need broad context while preserving spatial boundaries. DeepLab uses atrous features and multiscale class scores; this report checks their graphs and derivatives,then visibly fits compact V1/V2 models and evaluates fixed small-grid CRF refinement.
)
\toc

Source example: `examples/cpp/source/nn/1_convolutional_neural_networks/1.7_segmentation/deeplab_v1_v2.cpp`.

> The method

Dilated kernels enlarge receptive fields without extra weights. Dense ResNet suppresses strides after the requested output stride and increases dilation. V2 sums independent atrous score branches; fixed Gaussian/bilateral Potts mean-field messages optionally refine unary logits.

The editable concept diagram is `diagrams/deeplab_v1_v2_concept.tikz`. Regeneration uses
LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, plus dvisvgm; exports use the saved SVG.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/deeplab_v1_v2_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/deeplab_v1_v2_concept.tikz > build/deeplab_v1_v2_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/deeplab_v1_v2_concept.svg build/deeplab_v1_v2_concept.dvi > build/deeplab_v1_v2_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered local concept diagram.\n'
```
