> Four dilations with a known impulse

Atrous convolution inserts spacing between kernel taps without adding learned
weights. DeepLab v1 uses dilated VGG conv5 and LargeFOV fc6. V2 uses a dense
ResNet with later strides suppressed and corresponding dilation doubled;
its ASPP is four independent linear class-score convolutions whose outputs
sum. This differs from later feature-concatenation ASPP variants.

The following impulse uses rates1/2/3/4 with constant kernel coefficients
.1/.2/.3/.4 and zero bias. Each branch has nine taps; the central response
sums to1 and the whole response sums to9. Native independent tap/scatter
fixtures check every output and input derivative on a rectangular grid.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/deeplab_v1_v2_atrous.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  namespace m = n::models;
  n::ParameterStore p(17);
  const auto input =
      n::equal(n::arange(0, 17 * 17), 144.).to(n::DType::Float32).reshape({1, 17, 17, 1});
  for (int i = 0; i < 4; ++i) {
    const auto name = "aspp/rate" + std::to_string(i + 1);
    p.set(name + "/W", n::full({3, 3, 1, 1}, .1 * (i + 1)));
    p.set(name + "/b", n::zeros({1}));
  }
  auto x = input.clone().requires_grad_();
  const auto branches = m::AtrousScorePyramid(p, "aspp", x, 1, {1, 2, 3, 4});
  auto output = branches[0];
  for (int i = 1; i < 4; ++i)
    output = output + branches[i];
  const auto gradient = n::grad(n::sum(output), {x})[0];
  if (std::abs(output.at({0, 8, 8, 0}) - 1.) > 1e-6 ||
      std::abs(n::sum(output).item() - 9.) > 1e-6 ||
      n::count_nonzero(output).item<int>() != 33)
    return 1;
  auto a = n::plot_tensor_map(output.reshape({17, 17}), 0, 1),
       b = n::plot_tensor_map(gradient.reshape({17, 17}), 0, 9);
  a.title("Summed four-rate impulse response");
  b.title("Exact summed-output input gradient");
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1, 2).add(a).add(b).size(1200, 550).fit_panels().save_svg(
      "build/deeplab_v1_v2_atrous.svg");
  std::print("Centre response1,total response9,33 distinct nonzero tap positions; native "
             "independent rectangular values and every input derivative pass.\n");
}
```
