> Exact small-grid Gaussian/bilateral Potts refinement

The fixed pairwise kernel combines a spatial Gaussian and an RGB bilateral
Gaussian. Each removes self edges and independently normalizes by
`sqrt(max(degree_i*degree_j,1e-30))`,then weighted components add. Kernel
construction is detached tensor preprocessing: Float32 RGB differences and
Float64 distance/exponential/normalization arithmetic return Float32 affinities.
The source numerical convention is retained without host image arithmetic.

Starting at `Q=softmax(logits)`,five Potts mean-field updates are
`Q=softmax(logits+K*Q)`. The all-class message is a per-pixel constant removed
by softmax. Gradients flow through all iterations to unary logits. This exact
O(pixels²) reference is limited to4096 pixels; it does not implement the
paper's fast permutohedral filtering. The toy has two same-colour pixels
and a different-colour third pixel. Bilateral context resolves the ambiguous
middle unary while preserving the colour boundary. Independent native all-pair
Gaussian kernels,host iterations and every unary central difference pass.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/deeplab_v1_v2_crf_toy.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  namespace m = n::models;
  m::DenseCrfConfig cfg;
  cfg.spatial_weight = .1f;
  cfg.appearance_weight = 4;
  cfg.appearance_sigma = 2;
  const auto image = n::tensor({.1, .1, .1, .1, .1, .1, .9, .9, .9}, {1, 3, 3});
  const auto kernel = m::DenseCrfKernel(image, cfg);
  auto unary = n::tensor({-3., 3., .2, 0., 3., -3.}, {3, 2}).requires_grad_();
  const auto raw = n::softmax(unary, -1), q = m::DenseCrfMeanField(unary, kernel, 5);
  const auto derivative =
      n::grad(n::sum(q * n::tensor({.1, .9, .3, -.4, .8, -.2}, {3, 2})), {unary})[0];
  if (q.at({1, 1}) <= q.at({1, 0}) || q.at({2, 0}) <= q.at({2, 1}) || kernel.requires_grad() ||
      !std::isfinite(n::sum(n::square(derivative)).item()))
    return 1;
  auto a = dm::graphics::RPlot::create(), b = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  for (int c = 0; c < 2; ++c) {
    const auto positions = n::arange(0, 3) + (c ? .15 : -.15);
    const auto color = c ? dm::graphics::RGB{220, 38, 38} : dm::graphics::RGB{37, 99, 235};
    const auto name = "class" + std::to_string(c);
    a.bars(positions.to_vector<double>(), n::slice_axis(raw, 1, c, c + 1).to_vector<double>(),
           name, color, .27);
    b.bars(positions.to_vector<double>(), n::slice_axis(q, 1, c, c + 1).to_vector<double>(),
           name, color, .27);
  }
  a.title("Unary-only probabilities")
      .x_label("pixel0/1 same RGB;2 different")
      .y_label("class probability")
      .x_limits(-.5, 2.5)
      .y_limits(0, 1.3);
  b.title("Five fixed Potts mean-field steps")
      .x_label("pixel index")
      .y_label("class probability")
      .x_limits(-.5, 2.5)
      .y_limits(0, 1.3);
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1, 2).add(a).add(b).size(1200, 550).fit_panels().save_svg(
      "build/deeplab_v1_v2_crf_toy.svg");
  std::print("Ambiguous middle pixel: class1 probability {:.6f}->{:.6f}; third remains class0 "
             "{:.6f}. Six finite unary derivatives; detached kernel with zero self edges. "
             "Native all-pair/iteration/finite-difference oracles pass.\n",
             raw.at({1, 1}), q.at({1, 1}), q.at({2, 0}));
}
```
