> Full graphs and dense-backbone stride checks

Full V1 has20,505,429 learned scalars and32 learned tensor gradients,no BN
state. Full V2 uses ResNet101 and rates6/12/18/24,44,048,532 learned and
105,344 moving-state scalars,320 learned tensors. Both full forwards/backwards
execute below at33x33. Native stride32/16/8 ResNet18 checks preserve the same
176,712 learned/1,200 state count while changing stage resolution.

Compact V1 divides VGG widths by8,fc128/rate4 and disables dropout; it has
321,452 scalars. Compact V2 uses ResNet18/divisor8,rates1/2/3/4 and185,944
learned/1,200 state scalars. All compact tensor derivatives are nonzero in
native96-pixel checks. No pretrained weights or VOC accuracy is claimed.

```{cpp, results="markdown", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  namespace m = n::models;
  n::set_num_threads(2);
  for (bool v2 : {false, true}) {
    n::ParameterStore p(17), state(18);
    const auto x = n::sin(.13 * n::arange(0, 33 * 33 * 3)).reshape({1, 33, 33, 3});
    const auto net = v2 ? m::DeepLabV2(p, state, x, {}, true) : m::DeepLabV1(p, x, {}, true);
    const auto g = n::grad(n::mean(n::square(net.logits)), p.parameters());
    if (p.count() != (v2 ? 44048532 : 20505429) || state.count() != (v2 ? 105344 : 0) ||
        g.size() != (v2 ? 320 : 32) || net.logits.shape() != n::Shape{1, 33, 33, 21})
      return 1;
    for (const auto &v : g)
      if (!v.defined() || !std::isfinite(n::sum(n::square(v.to(n::DType::Float64))).item()))
        return 1;
    std::print("Full DeepLab v{}:{} learned/{} state scalars,all{} finite defined gradients "
               "at33px.\n",
               v2 ? 2 : 1, p.count(), state.count(), g.size());
  }
}
